  READ THIS BEFORE QUOTING THE RATIO.  The default average is tuned for a 64 MB image
  (A2 §4.4, owner question OQ2) and on a 100 KB machine image it cuts one to three
  chunks, shares nothing and costs the node overhead — the closed form says so and the
  row above measures it.  A checkpointing engine must therefore pick `avg` from the
  image size, not from a constant; that is a finding for the coordinator, not a knob
  this lane may turn (OQ2 fixed the default).  B7's own acceptance (<= 300 KB per
  checkpoint and >= 200x) is stated at 64 MB with a one-cell edit and is
  bench_checkpoint.ml's cell, not this one.

